--TEST--
Core\RateLimit::shed's window is bounded on both sides — the eighth arrival under a limit of eight is admitted and the ninth is shed, counted over one sweep — `rule:core-classes/ratelimit-two-members` and `rule:core-classes/ratelimit-gcra`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A bound asserted on both sides, over a *sweep* rather than off a line. § 2's
// GCRA admits a burst's worth at an instant and drains at `$limit` per `$per`,
// and with the burst defaulting to the limit exactly eight of these twelve
// arrivals fit. A limiter that spent its budget one arrival early — seven
// admitted, the eighth shed — prints the same word on the seventh line and on
// the ninth as a correct one does, so neither half of the bound says anything
// without the other. The two numbers are named together below, and the counts
// are what fail for the early limiter.
//
// An hour for eight is one unit every 450 seconds, so nothing measurable drains
// between these twelve calls: what is pinned here is the window, not the rate.
int $asked = 0;
int $admitted = 0;
int $shed = 0;
int $lastAdmitted = 0;
int $firstShed = 0;

// Two agreements ride along on the same sweep, because they are one decision
// read twice rather than a second question: `remaining` counts the budget down
// and then stays at zero, and `retryAfter` is absent exactly when the arrival
// was allowed (§ 3) rather than a zero the caller has to read as absence.
int $remainingAgreed = 0;
int $waitAgreed = 0;

foreach (Core\Arr::range(1, 12) as int $n) {
    var $decision = Core\RateLimit::shed("sweep:eight-per-hour", 8, 1h);
    $asked = $asked + 1;
    int $left = $decision->remaining() as int;
    if ($decision->allowed()) {
        $admitted = $admitted + 1;
        $lastAdmitted = $n;
        if ($left == 8 - $admitted) {
            $remainingAgreed = $remainingAgreed + 1;
        }
        if ($decision->retryAfter() == null) {
            $waitAgreed = $waitAgreed + 1;
        }
    } else {
        $shed = $shed + 1;
        if ($firstShed == 0) {
            $firstShed = $n;
        }
        // A refusal charges nothing, so there is nothing left to report and
        // nothing pushed further out either — the budget is spent, not
        // overdrawn.
        if ($left == 0) {
            $remainingAgreed = $remainingAgreed + 1;
        }
        if ($decision->retryAfter() != null) {
            $waitAgreed = $waitAgreed + 1;
        }
    }
}

// The counts, not the lines. `admitted` and `lastAdmitted` together also say
// the window does not reopen: an admission at the eleventh arrival would move
// the second number without moving the first.
echo "admitted ", $admitted, " and shed ", $shed, " of ", $asked, "\n";
echo "last admitted ", $lastAdmitted, ", first shed ", $firstShed, "\n";
echo "remaining agreed ", $remainingAgreed, " of ", $asked, "\n";
echo "retryAfter absent exactly when allowed ", $waitAgreed, " of ", $asked, "\n";
--EXPECT--
admitted 8 and shed 4 of 12
last admitted 8, first shed 9
remaining agreed 12 of 12
retryAfter absent exactly when allowed 12 of 12
